n, problem solving, responsibility), stress resilience adequate (responds to unexpected events), technical competence moderate (problem solving), decision quality unknown, attention accuracy high (concentration), crew cooperation questionable (arrogance, hot temper, weak leadership, loner), professional communication questionable, responsibility high, adaptability good.\n\nCandidate B: reliability high (conscientious), stress resilience high (handles stress well), technical competence moderate (weather assessment, computer skills), decision quality unknown, attention accuracy weak (weak memory for numbers), crew cooperation questionable (grumpy, uncooperative, nasty remarks), professional communication questionable, responsibility unknown, adaptability unknown.\n\nCandidate C: reliability high (100% reliable), stress resilience high (keeps calm), technical competence high (understands complicated technology), decision quality high (quick correct decisions), attention accuracy unknown, crew cooperation positive (creates positive atmosphere), professional communication difficulty, responsibility unknown, adaptability unknown.\n\nCandidate A: reliability moderate (anticipate dangerous, leadership), stress resilience unknown, technical competence high (spatial vision, complex connections), decision quality unknown, attention accuracy unknown, crew cooperation questionable (show-off, not open to new ideas, not good at criticism), professional communication questionable, responsibility unknown, adaptability questionable.\n\nGiven this, Candidate C seems strong across many criteria, except communication difficulty and egocentric. But he creates positive atmosphere with crew, which may offset communication difficulty? However difficulty communicating ideas could be safety-critical. Egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nCandidate D has strong reliability but interpersonal issues. Candidate B also has interpersonal issues and attention issues. Candidate C seems best overall, but we need to bring evidence: known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. We can argue that his positive crew atmosphere and reliability outweigh communication issues, which could be mitigated.\n\nThus we could shift recommendation to Candidate C. That would bring new candidate into discussion, covering under-discussed candidate. That aligns with requirement to cover all candidates before final. So we can propose Candidate C as a stronger alternative to D and B.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: \"While I see the concerns about D and B, I think Candidate C offers a more balanced profile.\" Provide evidence: 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical competence. Acknowledge concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, but argue that crew atmosphere is positive and decision quality is high.\n\nThus we will vote Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: mention we appreciate points, but propose C, with reasoning. Then METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
